## OPTIMISTIC CLAIM SAFETY

Allocator entries are hints. Atomic create-if-absent is the race primitive.

For portfolio work:
`next_generation = pin_generation + 1`
`claim_path = coordination/portfolio/pins/<job_id>/G<next_generation_6d>.json`

For normal opportunities:
`claim_path = coordination/opportunities/claims/<opportunity_id>.json`

Do not pre-read those directories. CREATE first.

After winning, validate exact current job state before substantive mutation. If the allocator hint became stale, do no substantive mutation; write a bounded stale-hint abort/return and immediately re-enter fast allocation.

Ready unowned work outranks recovery because it is cheaper and less ambiguous. Recovery is attempted only after clean ready work is exhausted.

If allocator age is >90s, skip recovery instead of manually reconstructing liveness.

## AFTER OWNERSHIP

Now load only what the exact job needs, including when applicable:
- portfolio PIN + worker contract;
- Guide/Metabolism for claimed guide work;
- verification/critic controls;
- Master Context for strategic/root work;
- page plate/request/publication laws for `AAA000` scope;
- Live Page Watch only for human-visible page changes.

Then:
- execute through definition of done;
- re-fetch/CAS mutable targets;
- heartbeat during longer work;
- RETURN durably with evidence/tests/changed paths/residuals;
- materialize grounded successors when authorized;
- re-enter fast allocation in the SAME chat after RETURN.

## GUIDE / RESCATE

Guide is a worker role, not a privileged chat. A claimed guide job may be `GUIDE_PLANNER`, `GUIDE_INTEGRATOR`, `GUIDE_RESCATE`, `GUIDE_CRITIC` or `GUIDE_STEWARD`.

Guide work must change durable reality, not just analyse. `RESCATE` means remove a bottleneck/connect a cable/make work claimable/reduce duplication or human routing.

Do not invent filler because capacity exceeds useful work. Surplus capacity ends quickly in `NO_ALLOCATION`.

## RECOVERY

Recovery applies only to previously owned work:
- no PIN/claim -> no recovery;
- <6m latest owned signal -> active;
- 6–10m -> suspect;
- >=10m + retry-safe -> recovery candidate;
- newest valid pin generation is authoritative.

